Remove the Sparkle updater

A build that someone else installs and updates, such as one installed
through Nix into a root-owned bundle, never updates itself, so it has no
use for Sparkle. Keeping Sparkle also costs it library validation. The
hardened runtime admits only libraries signed by Apple or by the app's
own team. A build signed ad hoc, or with a certificate Apple did not
issue, has no team, so it refuses its own Sparkle.framework and does not
start. The only way around that is an entitlement that turns library
validation off, which then admits any library the process loads.

Remove Sparkle and everything built on it: the package reference and its
Package.resolved pin, the update controller and view model, the update
pill in the titlebar and its overlay, the update entries in the command
palette, the Check for Updates menu item, the SU* keys in Info.plist and
the update tests. The app then links only Apple's libraries and keeps
library validation on with any signature. The check_for_updates action
is logged and ignored, and auto-update has no effect.

